      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.046,
            0.347,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.271,
            0.106
          ],
          "content": "So, ∠1 = ∠2."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.106,
            0.679,
            0.125
          ],
          "content": "Thus, by the AAS congruence condition, ∆BAD ≅ ∆DCB."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.124,
            0.847,
            0.162
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, AD = CB, and DC = BA, since these are corresponding sides of congruent triangles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.164,
            0.548,
            0.187
          ],
          "content": "Is it wrong to write ∆BAD ≅ ∆CDB? Why?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.189,
            0.848,
            0.264
          ],
          "content": "Thus, we have established that if all the angles of a quadrilateral are right angles, then the opposite sides have equal lengths. Therefore, the quadrilateral is a rectangle. Thus, a rectangle can simply be defined as follows —"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.268,
            0.846,
            0.312
          ],
          "content": "**Rectangle:** A rectangle is a quadrilateral in which the angles are all 90°. Let us list the properties of a rectangle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.316,
            0.621,
            0.337
          ],
          "content": "**Property 1:** All the angles of a rectangle are 90°."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.341,
            0.691,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": "**Property 2:** The opposite sides of a rectangle are equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.371,
            0.606,
            0.393
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "？ Are the opposite sides of a rectangle parallel?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.396,
            0.847,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": "They definitely seem so. This fact can be justified using one of the transversal properties."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.434,
            0.558,
            0.47
          ],
          "content": "Notice that AB acts as a transversal to AD and BC, and that $\\angle \\mathbf{A} + \\angle \\mathbf{B} = 90^{\\circ} + 90^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.47,
            0.56,
            0.562
          ],
          "content": "When the sum of the internal angles on the same side of the transversal is 180°, the lines are parallel. We can use this fact to conclude that the lines AD and BC are parallel, which we represent as AD || BC."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.562,
            0.559,
            0.6
          ],
          "content": "Can you similarly show that AB is parallel to DC (AB||DC)?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.564,
            0.434,
            0.893,
            0.588
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_8_image_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.604,
            0.844,
            0.626
          ],
          "content": "**Property 3:** The opposite sides of a rectangle are parallel to each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.628,
            0.847,
            0.667
          ],
          "content": "**Property 4:** The diagonals of a rectangle are of equal length and they bisect each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.674,
            0.394,
            0.696
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "A Special Rectangle"
        },
        {
